{"n": 603, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "603.webp", "text": "32-54\n\nTESTING INSTRUCTIONS A\n\nAtter finishing the flashing code call, always disconnect the battery for troubleshooting and cover the negative pole or terminal, Make tests with a BMW Service\nTester or Digital Tester Il at room temperature. Using different testers could activate the airbag. Pull off the alrbag diagnosis plug.\n\nAfter finishing repairs the last step would be connecting the battery again and checking the function of the system.\n\ni there was a brief detect, cancel the memory of the diagnosis unit by disconnecting and connecting the battery. Check pertinent parts. for tight fit and damage\nwith the ignition on. Replace pertinent parts, If a tault Is displayed.\n\nFault Code A or B = Higher or lower resistance In gray-white/gray Fault Code A:\nwire to airbag unit. Measure resistance of wire\nagainst car ground.\n\nResistarice 200 to 600 ohms? ——— yes —— See Fault Code H.\nDisconnect plug for diagnosis unit. —__—_—_——- yes if\n\nConnect airbag test plug 62 1 260 no\n\nand check wire with an ohmmeter. !\n\n3.0 to 5.0 ohms? Replace diagnosis unit.\n| Fault Code B:\n\nno Replace diagnosis unit.\nDisconnect plug (behind cap on steering yes ——— Replace wire.\ncolumn). Connect airbag test plug\n\n62 1 260 and check wire with an ohm-\n\nmeter.\n\n3.0 to 5.0 ohms?\n\nno\n\nTake airbag untt out of steering wheel and ——— yes ——— Replace airbag unit.\n\npull off plug. Connect wires of airbag test\nplug 62 1 260 and measure resistance on\ndisconnected plug with two test points.\n1.4 to 1.8 ohms?\n\nReplace contact ring.", "words": [["32-54", 0.4787, 0.0279, 0.5446, 0.0524], ["TESTING", 0.1013, 0.0995, 0.1444, 0.1227], ["INSTRUCTIONS", 0.1499, 0.0995, 0.2285, 0.1227], ["A", 0.234, 0.0995, 0.2432, 0.1227], ["Atter", 0.1039, 0.1333, 0.1272, 0.1446], ["finishing", 0.1307, 0.1333, 0.1738, 0.1472], ["the", 0.1773, 0.134, 0.1935, 0.1446], ["flashing", 0.1966, 0.1333, 0.2361, 0.1472], ["code", 0.2396, 0.134,